{% comment %}
  InstaMom University — the shipping-window promise, shown under the buy buttons
  on a product page.

  Owner's launch copy, verbatim:
    "Orders will ship as soon as possible but no later than 7-10 business days.
     As supply chains shift some items may be replaced with similar items of
     equal value."
    "Pre-order now, all Welcome Boxes begin shipping on Friday August 14th, 2026"

  Both sentences are promises, so they have to agree with the Shipping &
  Delivery Policy (7–10 business days processing, and the substitution clause in
  its §8). If one changes, change the other — shopify/content/policy-shipping.html.

  The 14 August date is scoped to `pre-order` + `welcome-week`, which today is
  the Welcome Week Starter alone. Warm Hug from Home is also pre-order but ships
  from its own ready stock, so it must NOT inherit a Welcome-box date, and a
  coming-soon box must not show a ship date at all.

  ⚠ 14 August 2026 is a fixed date in this snippet. Once it passes, the line
  reads as stale rather than reassuring — remove it, or replace it with the next
  shipping date.

  Usage: {% render 'instamom-shipping-note', product: product %}
  Styling: .instamom-shipnote* in assets/instamom.css
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign is_preorder = false
  assign is_welcome = false
  if product.tags contains 'pre-order'
    assign is_preorder = true
  endif
  if product.tags contains 'welcome-week'
    assign is_welcome = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="instamom-shipnote">
  {%- if is_preorder and is_welcome -%}
    <p class="instamom-shipnote__lead">
      <strong>Pre-order now</strong> &mdash; all Welcome Boxes begin shipping on
      <strong>Friday, August 14, 2026</strong>.
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
  <p class="instamom-shipnote__body">
    Orders ship as soon as possible, and no later than 7&ndash;10 business days.
    As supply chains shift, some items may be replaced with similar items of
    equal value.
  </p>
</div>
